A \textbf{partition} of the interval $[a, b]$ is a finite set of points:
\[
P = \{x_0, x_1, x_2, \ldots, x_n\}
\]

where:
\[
a = x_0 < x_1 < x_2 < \cdots < x_{n-1} < x_n = b
\]

This divides $[a, b]$ into $n$ subintervals:
\[
[x_0, x_1], \quad [x_1, x_2], \quad \ldots, \quad [x_{n-1}, x_n]
\]

\textbf{Width of $i$-th subinterval:}
\[
\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}
\]

\textbf{Regular Partition:} All subintervals have equal width:
\[
\Delta x = \frac{b-a}{n}
\]

\textcolor{primaryblue}{\faInfoCircle\ \textbf{Sample Points:}}

In each subinterval $[x_{i-1}, x_i]$, choose a sample point $x_i^*$ where $x_{i-1} \leq x_i^* \leq x_i$.

Common choices:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Left endpoint:} $x_i^* = x_{i-1}$
    \item \textbf{Right endpoint:} $x_i^* = x_i$
    \item \textbf{Midpoint:} $x_i^* = \frac{x_{i-1} + x_i}{2}$
\end{itemize}

