\vspace{0.5cm}

\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{Problem:}} Find the volume of the solid obtained by rotating the region bounded by $y = \sqrt{x}$, $y = 0$, $x = 0$, and $x = 4$ about the $x$-axis.

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{Solution:}}

\textbf{Step 1:} Identify the setup

Rotating about $x$-axis, so use disk method with radius $r = f(x) = \sqrt{x}$.

\textbf{Step 2:} Set up integral

\begin{align*}
V &= \int_0^4 \pi [\sqrt{x}]^2 \, dx \\
&= \int_0^4 \pi x \, dx
\end{align*}

\textbf{Step 3:} Evaluate

\begin{align*}
V &= \pi \left[\frac{x^2}{2}\right]_0^4 \\
&= \pi \left(\frac{16}{2} - 0\right) \\
&= 8\pi
\end{align*}

\textbf{Answer:} \boxed{V = 8\pi \text{ cubic units}}

\vspace{0.5cm}

If the region between two curves $y = f(x)$ and $y = g(x)$ (where $f(x) \geq g(x) \geq 0$) on $[a, b]$ is rotated about the $x$-axis, the volume is:
\[
\boxed{V = \int_a^b \pi \left([f(x)]^2 - [g(x)]^2\right) \, dx}
\]

\textcolor{primaryblue}{\faInfoCircle\ \textbf{Think of it as:}}
\[
V = \int_a^b \pi \left(R^2 - r^2\right) \, dx
\]

where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $R = f(x)$ is the outer radius
    \item $r = g(x)$ is the inner radius
\end{itemize}

\textcolor{primaryblue}{\faInfoCircle\ \textbf{Why ``Washer''?}}

Each cross-section is a disk with a hole (like a washer). The area is:
\[
A = \pi R^2 - \pi r^2 = \pi(R^2 - r^2)
\]

